# Adic completions at places and their functoriality

Definition: `AlgebraicCurve_PlaceCompletion` (`167709dd-ccd9-51e3-a47c-f878cec56c75`), by Claude,
2026-09-05.

Throughout, a place $V$ of a field extension $F/K$ is the project's `Place K F`: a valuation subring
$\mathcal O_V\subseteq F$ containing $\operatorname{im}(K\to F)$, proper in $F$ and a principal
ideal ring, hence a discrete valuation ring, with `heightOneSpectrum` its maximal ideal,
`adicValuation` the induced $\mathbb Z^{m0}$-valued valuation on $F$ and `ord` minus its logarithm.
Here `adicCompletion` and `adicCompletionIntegers` name the completion $\hat F_V$ of $F$ at that
height-one prime and its valuation subring $\hat{\mathcal O}_V$, in Mathlib's sense.

For $K\subseteq F\subseteq F'$ with $F'/F$ integral and a place $W$ of $F'$, write
$V=W.\mathrm{restrict}\,F$ (the contraction of $\mathcal O_W$ along $F\to F'$) and
$e=W.\mathrm{ramificationIndex}\,F$ (the least positive value attained by $\mathrm{ord}_W$ on
nonzero elements of $F$). The valuation identity $v_W(\iota x)=v_V(x)^e$ is proved on $F$, then on
the `WithVal` models, where the induced map is shown uniformly continuous; completing it gives the
ring homomorphism `kw_ffgc_adicCompletionComap` $\hat F_V\to\hat{F'}_W$, continuous, compatible with
the coercions from $F$, and satisfying $v(\varphi x)=v(x)^e$; it carries $\hat{\mathcal O}_V$ into
$\hat{\mathcal O}_W$, whence a map of integer rings and the corresponding algebra structures, scalar
towers and continuity of scalar multiplication. Further declarations: a rank-one structure on the
valuation of $\hat F_V$ coming from its discreteness (base $2$), the real absolute value
$y\mapsto\lVert y\rVert^{1/e}$ on $\hat{F'}_W$, compatibility of the two algebra maps out of $F$,
the $\hat F_V$-linear map sending a family of coefficients to the corresponding combination of the
images of an $F$-basis of $F'$, its dense range, finite-dimensionality of $\hat{F'}_W$ over $\hat
F_V$ when $[F':F]<\infty$, the trace $\operatorname{Tr}_{\hat{F'}_W/\hat F_V}$ and its $F$-linear
restriction along $F'\to\hat{F'}_W$. Finally: $v_V$ of the image of $x\in F$ equals
$V.\mathrm{adicValuation}\,x$; the image lies in $\hat{\mathcal O}_V$ exactly when $x\in\mathcal
O_V$; every element of $\hat F_V$ differs from an element of $F$ by an element of $\hat{\mathcal
O}_V$; and $K$ maps into $\hat{\mathcal O}_V$, giving $\hat{\mathcal O}_V$ a $K$-algebra structure.
A general instance makes any $K$-algebra an algebra over a valuation subring of $K$.

**Relation to Mathlib.** The completion and its integers are Mathlib's
`IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.adicCompletion` for the maximal ideal of the valuation ring of a
`Place`; `Place`, its `restrict` and `ramificationIndex` are the project's own notions, and the map
between completions along `restrict`, together with the associated algebra and trace structure, is
built here.

**Where it is used.** These definitions supply the local vocabulary (completions at places,
ramification indices, local traces and approximation by global elements) used in the project's
treatment of divisors and residues on curves, which feeds the modular-curve part of the argument.

<!-- Generated by add_prove2me_provenance.py -->
